course: dictionary
lesson: 10524
title: Typical: usual, or a good example
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Typical is a word you will meet in every subject. It means usual and normal for a certain kind of person, thing or place. Look at «a typical school day»: the words around it tell you it means the sort of day that happens most often at school, not a special one.
explain: Typical can also mean a good example of its kind. In science, «a typical insect has six legs», so a typical insect shows the main features that insects share. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes typical is a complaint. If it rains on sports day and you say, «Typical!», you mean it happened again, just as you expected. The exclamation mark and the story around it show the feeling, so read the clues carefully.
explain: Typical has related words too: «typical of» and «typically». They all come from the same idea of what is usual for something.
fact: Typical is an adjective, and it has the forms more typical and most typical.
fact: «Typical» means usual and normal for a certain kind of person, thing or place.
fact: «Typical» also means showing the main features of its kind, a good example.
fact: «Typical!» is said when something annoying happens again, as you expected.
fact: «A typical bacterium is about 1 to 2 thousandths of a millimetre long.» Here typical tells you the size of a normal example.
exercise: In science, «a typical insect has six legs.» What does typical mean here? | Shiny and brand new | Very small and hard to see | *Showing the main features of its kind | Hidden under the ground
exercise: «Typical! It's raining on sports day again.» What does Typical! show? | *The rain happened again, just as you expected | The day has been cancelled for good | Someone has won a prize
exercise: In «a typical school day», what does typical mean? | A day that is very wet | A day for a test | *Usual and normal for school | A day with no lessons
test: «Microbes are living things too small to see with the eye alone; a typical bacterium is about 1 to 2 thousandths of a millimetre long.» What does a typical bacterium mean? | An unusual bacterium, bigger than all the others | *A normal, usual example of a bacterium's size | A bacterium that is not alive | A bacterium that you can see with your eye
test: Sam says, «Chatbots have a typical style, with words like furthermore.» What does typical style suggest? | *A style that shows the usual features of chatbots | A style that changes every day | A style that nobody has ever seen | A style that is hand-written
exam: Which sentence uses typical to mean a good example of its kind? | «Typical! The bus is late again.» | *«A typical desert plant stores water in its stem.» | «The typical school day ended early today, which was surprising.»
